      "classes": "1: MATCH 1 -- Both denote an air plenum.\n2: NO MATCH -- No candidate is an air quality sensor.\n3: MATCH 2 -- Both denote a desired temperature value for control.\n4: MATCH 4 -- Both denote a temperature deadband setpoint.\n5: NO MATCH -- No candidate is a packaged heat pump.\n6: NO MATCH -- No candidate is a condensing unit.\n7: NO MATCH -- No candidate is a humidifier.\n8: NO MATCH -- No candidate is an isolation valve.\n9: NO MATCH -- No candidate is a space heater.\n10: NO MATCH -- No candidate is a dry cooler.",
      "relationships": "1: MATCH 7 -- Having a fan expresses the part relationship.\n2: MATCH 8 -- Having a filter expresses the part relationship.\n3: MATCH 9 -- Having a damper expresses the part relationship.\n4: MATCH 11 -- Having a cooling valve expresses the part relationship.\n5: MATCH 10 -- Having a heating valve expresses the part relationship.\n6: MATCH 12 -- Having an economizer expresses the part relationship.\n7: MATCH 13 -- Both link the unit to its air temperature sensor point.\n8: MATCH 19 -- Both link the unit to its CO2 sensor point.\n9: MATCH 14 -- Both link the unit to its air temperature setpoint.\n10: MATCH 15 -- Both link the unit to its cooling temperature setpoint.\n11: MATCH 16 -- Both link the unit to its heating temperature setpoint.\n12: MATCH 20 -- Both link the thermostat to its temperature sensor point.\n13: MATCH 6 -- Both link the zone to its occupancy sensor point.\n14: NO MATCH -- No candidate locates the sensor in a building.\n15: MATCH 1 -- A building containing a floor expresses the part relationship.\n16: MATCH 2 -- A floor containing a space expresses the part relationship.\n17: MATCH 3 -- Including a zone expresses the building–zone part relationship.\n18: NO MATCH -- Assignment to a zone does not necessarily mean serving it.\n19: MATCH 17 -- Both link the unit to its outside-air CO2 sensor point.\n20: MATCH 18 -- Both link the unit to its return-air CO2 sensor point.",
      "properties": "1: MATCH \"reading\" -- Both denote the measured temperature.\n2: NO MATCH -- A reading is a measurement, not the sensor's status.\n3: MATCH \"reading\" -- Both denote the measured air temperature.\n4: MATCH \"reading\" -- Both denote the measured CO2 level.\n5: MATCH \"reading\" -- Both denote the measured outside-air CO2 level.\n6: MATCH \"reading\" -- Both denote the measured return-air CO2 level.\n7: MATCH \"occupancy\" -- Both denote the sensed occupied state.\n8: MATCH \"reading\" -- Both denote the measured CO2 differential.\n9: MATCH \"reading\" -- Both denote the measured water temperature.",
